 prf-story\">As of Oct 12, the record on the middle value of the county&rsquo;s 13 grids runs from 1951 to 2025, and May to June came in under 90% of normal in 44 of those 75 years. In 2025 the middle of the grids got 29% of normal in April to May and 199% in September to October. Every grid listed had its driest year in 2013, with grid 20732 at 22% of normal. A preliminary estimate for August to September 2026 on grid 21033 reads 23.0, an estimate from NOAA rain and not RMA&rsquo;s final index.</p>"}
